      "content": [
        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": [],
          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"balzac-illusions-perdues-6f5451dc60a8ce78\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":0,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Lucien’s utterance is primarily a forceful avowal that he loves his friends, offered to rebut their charge that vanity and selfishness infect his friendship. It presents the depth of his affection as true. It contains no distinct undertaking or commitment, and the exclamatory framing supplies intensity but not independent evidence that the love words function as a reflex-like expressive discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The narrative casts doubt on the depth, stability, and practical consequences of Lucien’s professed love, but this affects sincerity and characterization rather than the utterance’s truth-conditional mode.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Lucien directly tells his assembled friends, in response to their criticism, that they do not know how much he loves them.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The avowal is defensive: Lucien invokes his affection after his friends interpret his eager repayment of their aid as vanity and latent selfishness. They answer that love should be demonstrated through participation in their ethos of generous friendship, implicitly challenging not necessarily the existence of affection but its quality and behavioral force. Lucien subsequently concedes that they are right, while the narrator emphasizes his capacity for contradictory resolutions and facile movement across feelings. This creates possible self-deception or unstable sincerity, without changing the core utterance into anything other than an emphatic avowal.\",\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"« Oh! mon Dieu, s'écria Lucien, vous ne savez donc pas combien je vous aime. »\",\"supports\":\"The embedded love clause explicitly presents Lucien’s strong affection for his friends as true, strongly supporting T. The exclamatory reporting marks emotional delivery but does not independently establish E.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Fulgence has just accused Lucien of putting vanity into friendship and calls such vanity evidence of « un effroyable égoïsme » that poisons friendship.\",\"supports\":\"Lucien’s avowal functions as a defensive answer to a challenge about the genuineness and quality of his friendship.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"The friends reply: « Si tu nous aimais comme nous nous aimons, aurais-tu mis tant d'empressement et tant d'emphase à nous rendre ce que nous avions tant de plaisir à te donner? »\",\"supports\":\"The interlocutors test the avowal against Lucien’s conduct; their challenge concerns the depth or practical realization of his love, not a separate commitment enacted by the words themselves.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"After their admonition, « Lucien baissa la tête: ses amis avaient raison »; later the narrator says his temperament « parcourait si facilement le clavier des sentiments » and produced contradictory resolutions.\",\"supports\":\"The narration introduces doubt about Lucien’s self-understanding, constancy, and sincerity while leaving the utterance’s avowal-like semantic force intact.\",\"confidence\":0.97}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the core as an emphatic avowal. Its defensive purpose, questionable sincerity, and emotionally exclamatory delivery are contextual features adequately described without adding P, E, or O.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
        }
